[0.0031,1.0],[0.0,1.0],[0.0,0.0]]],"settings":"$G = 1$, $\\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$, $\\phi = 0$","input":"$m(v) = 0$ for $v < 0$ and $M$ for $v > 0$, with $r_s = 2GM/c^2$: a shell of null dust of mass $M$ falling in along $v = 0$.","caption":["This is the plane of $v$ and $r$ at $\\theta = \\pi/2$ and $\\phi = 0$, drawn with $cv - r$ up so that the ingoing rays, $v$ constant, run at 45°. A shell of null dust of mass $M$ falls in along $v = 0$: before it $m = 0$ and the metric is flat, and after it $m = M$ and the metric is Schwarzschild's in ingoing coordinates, with $g^{rr} = 1 - r_s/r$. The outgoing rays run at 45° until the shell reaches them and bend away from $r_s$ after.","The event horizon is the outgoing ray that reaches $r_s$ just as the shell does and stays there. It leaves the centre at $cv = -2r_s$, before the shell arrives, and crosses flat space, so an outgoing ray that leaves the centre after that moment ends at $r = 0$ even though its first stretch is flat. Behind the shell every future cone inside $r_s$ points to smaller $r$, and $r = 0$ is where the Kretschmann scalar $48G^2m^2/c^4r^6$ diverges."],"source":{"fields":["coords","parameters","metric_components","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","domains"],"version":"e919f221603610eb"}}],"eddington_finkelstein_outgoing":[{"id":"shell","label":"an exploding shell","plane":["u","r"],"families":["ingoing","outgoing"],"xlabel":"$r/r_s$","ylabel":"$(cu + r)/r_s$","ticks":{"x":[{"at":0.0,"label":"$0$"},{"at":1.0,"label":"$1$"},{"at":2.0,"label":"$2$"},{"at":3.0,"label":"$3$"},{"at":4.0,"label":"$4$"}],"y":[{"at":-1.0,"label":"$-1$"},{"at":0.0,"label":"$0$"},{"at":1.0,"label":"$1$"},{"at":2.0,"label":"$2$"}]},"box":[0,4,-1.5,2.5],"to_display":[[0.0,1.0],[1.0,1.0]],"mirror":false,"rays":{"P":[[[0.0159,-0.0203],[0.0333,0.001],[0.0493,0.0234],[0.0653,0.0488],[0.0797,0.0751],[0.0939,0.1043],[0.1076,0.1365],[0.1198,0.1693],[0.1316,0.2049],[0.1428,0.2433],[0.1527,0.282],[0.1714,0.3701],[0.1872,0.4663],[0.2